  "decision_conditions": [
    "Occupier",
    "The development must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date hereof.\r\rReason: To comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended.",
    "All external facing materials, treatments and finishes shall be similar to those of the original building and maintained and retained thereafter. This applies unless differences are shown on the drawings we have approved. \r\rReason: To ensure that the extension harmonises with the existing building and to ensure compliance with Policy 28 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "The development must be carried out in accordance with the provisions of the Fire Safety Strategy.\r\rReason: To ensure that the development incorporates the necessary fire safety measures in accordance with the Mayor's London Plan Policy D12.",
    "The extension hereby permitted shall be used only as an ancillary extension incidental to the enjoyment of the main dwellinghouse and for no other purposes. To ensure the ancillary nature of the outbuilding it shall not have:\r\ri) a separate postal address,\rii) separate metres for the provision of services,\riii) a separate and registered Land Registry title, \riv) a separate Council tax account,\rv) a separate access independent of the main dwelling house.\r\rReason: To ensure the ancillary nature of the extension to the main dwelling house and to ensure that the extension hereby permitted is not used as a separate unit of residential accommodation or for purposes other than that incidental to the enjoyment of the main dwellinghouse to protect the amenities of adjoining occupiers in accordance with policy 29 of the Sutton Local Plan."
  ],
